i><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Added scenery details</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >High-definition assets</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Achievements and optional challenges</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Steam version is also planned to receive the following exclusive updates in future:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Multiplayer game modes</strong> for shared drives or competitive gameplay</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Access to <strong>extra locations</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Access to a <strong>broader range of vehicles</strong>,<strong>\u00a0</strong>including combustion engines</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enhanced graphics features such as <strong>post-processing effects</strong> and <strong>added environmental detail</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Active independent development</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Slow Roads is a living project with new features, locations, and vehicles in continuous development. The roadmap is long, but the upcoming priorities are:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New locations, featuring mountains, oceans, tunnels, and more</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >More vehicles, with improved physics</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Improved graphics features for lighting, weather, and environmental detail</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>* Force feedback support is targeted for release but remains in experimental development, so cannot be guaranteed at this time</i></p>",
